WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.398 --> 00:00:04.054
Unit fourteen. Understanding Boolean Logic!

2
00:00:05.047 --> 00:00:09.431
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.481 --> 00:00:13.075
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:17.447
Today we learn about Understanding Boolean Logic. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.536 --> 00:00:23.269
Boolean logic. Say it with me. Boolean logic!

6
00:00:26.786 --> 00:00:29.746
AND. Say it with me. AND!

7
00:00:33.248 --> 00:00:36.415
OR. Say it with me. OR!

8
00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:43.255
NOT. Say it with me. NOT!

9
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:50.550
True/false. Say it with me. True/false!

10
00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:58.742
Logical operator. Say it with me. Logical operator!

11
00:01:02.209 --> 00:01:06.968
Condition combination. Say it with me. Condition combination!

12
00:01:10.475 --> 00:01:15.344
Decision-making. Say it with me. Decision-making!

13
00:01:18.835 --> 00:01:27.841
Boolean logic uses a logical operator like AND, OR, and NOT to combine a true/false condition. This supports complex decision-making in programming.

14
00:01:27.891 --> 00:01:31.076
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.219
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:37.269 --> 00:01:38.243
OR!

17
00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:44.158
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:45.993
Condition combination!

19
00:01:46.999 --> 00:01:54.904
Did you know? Boolean logic is named after mathematician George Boole and forms the foundation of how all computers make decisions!

20
00:01:54.954 --> 00:01:57.066
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:58.246 --> 00:02:09.284
Think and answer. Can you think of a real-life sentence that uses 'AND' or 'OR' the same way boolean logic does?

22
00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:10.484
Great answer!

23
00:02:11.618 --> 00:02:16.764
